# `SEQUENCE-GENRE-VOCABULARY`: `sequence` is surface that `figdown 0.3` does not
# have, so a 0.3 document naming it is a line error — and NOT `unknown genre`,
# which would send the author hunting a typo that is not there. core §13.7
# forbids reinterpreting a document under a version other than the one it
# declares, so the engine may not quietly promote this file to 0.4; it says
# which version the genre needs and stops. NO CODE WAS WRITTEN FOR THIS: the
# later-version search `STATECHART-GENRE-SCOPE` added for `statechart` (fixture 231) answers the
# second case on its own, which is what this fixture is really pinning.
# Second header: the same genre at 0.4 is fine.
figdown 0.3 sequence
figdown 0.4 sequence
